    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "749532d2_375700e5",
        "filename": "core/cortex-m/mpu.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 102,
      "author": {
        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-29T06:12:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think it\u0027s worth moving this to a common file. It replaces a use of __builtin_clz for the same purpose and is broken out to a function just so the assertion can help catch misuse, but other potential users might want to do something different if given 0 as input.",
      "parentUuid": "9991473f_3b9988a1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 97,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 102,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "597230422d28a1775ef73f4a06e98a31bcb2f345",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "edd5e4a1_cd77d8ba",
        "filename": "core/cortex-m/mpu.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 102,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-30T00:21:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think there\u0027s value in giving a more readable name to __builtin_ctz and checking for misuse since it\u0027s not entirely obvious. If, in the future, there\u0027s a better way to implement it (e.g., custom assembly), then it\u0027s easy to update and test in a single place. This is effectively the same reason for having the other one-liners that exist in util.h.\n\nEven if the unit tests don\u0027t run on device, they can still run on the host (which the tests in utils.c do), which is better than nothing.",
      "parentUuid": "749532d2_375700e5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 97,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 102,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "597230422d28a1775ef73f4a06e98a31bcb2f345",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
